{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"384169f4-ab6b-480a-935a-383290b272c6","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Slope-intercept form describes a line using its starting height on the vertical axis and its rate of change.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Slope-intercept form"},{"op":"equation","id":"form","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=mx+b"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-1,4],"y":[-1,9],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"line","y":"2*x+1","domain":[-1,4]}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"384169f4-ab6b-480a-935a-383290b272c6","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The intercept b is the value of y when x is zero. This line crosses the vertical axis at one.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"intercept","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":{"on":"line","x":0},"label":"(0, 1)"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"bvalue","anchor":{"el":"form","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x=0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ y=b=1"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"384169f4-ab6b-480a-935a-383290b272c6","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Slope is rise divided by run. From the intercept, move one unit right and two units up to reach the line again.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"slope","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"next","at":{"on":"line","x":1},"label":"(1, 3)"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"start"},"to":[1,1],"arrow":true,"stroke":"dashed","label":"run = 1"},{"kind":"segment","from":[1,1],"to":{"at":"next"},"arrow":true,"stroke":"dashed","label":"rise = 2"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"mvalue","anchor":{"el":"bvalue","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"m=\\frac{\\text{rise}}{\\text{run}}=\\frac{2}{1}=2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"384169f4-ab6b-480a-935a-383290b272c6","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Putting slope two and intercept one into the form gives y equals two x plus one. Another equal step reaches two, five.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"mvalue","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\boxed{y=2x+1}"},{"op":"figure","id":"extend","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"third","at":{"on":"line","x":2},"label":"(2, 5)"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"next"},"to":[2,3],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,3],"to":{"at":"third"},"stroke":"dashed"}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"For y = 2x + 1, what is y when x = 3?","expected_gist":"y = 7: multiply 3 by the slope 2, then add the intercept 1."}}}
